However, a dedicated adversary could deposit enough collateral assets to reach the
minting limit and immediately withdraw enough MONO to reach the redeeming limit in the
same transaction; this would exhaust the limits of a given duration window, preventing all
subsequent users from entering and exiting the system. Additionally, if the duration is long
(e.g., a few hours or a day), such attacks would cause the PSM contract to become unusable
for extended periods of time. It is important to note that adversaries conducting such
attacks would incur the fee imposed on redemption operations, making the attack less
appealing.

Fix Analysis
This issue has not been unresolved. The Ondo Finance team has acknowledged the issue
and plans to keep the values of resetMintDuration and resetRedeemDuration
reasonably small to prevent DoS attacks. However, the code remains unchanged at the
time of writing.

