Severity: Medium
Difficulty: Low
Type: Data Validation

Description:
The Metadata::validate method computes the serialized size of each tensor by
multiplying the size of the data by the product of the tensor’s dimensions. Since Rust does
not check for integer overflows in release builds, this computation may overflow and
produce the wrong result.

 fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), SafeTensorError> {
 let mut start = 0;
 for (i, info) in self.tensors.iter().enumerate() {
