Description:
The code in figure 5.1 always produces an error. Unnecessary error messages could cause
user fatigue, which could make users more likely to ignore necessary errors.

Specifically, the code in figure 5.1 constructs an Expression::Equal. That expression is
passed to the eval_const_rational function, which executes specific code depending
on the type of expression passed to it. eval_const_rational does not have a case to
handle Expression::Equal, so it returns an error.

