This enabling and disabling of staking could lead to unexpected behavior; for example, if
the stakeAmount is set to 0 when a layer zero edge is already created with a stake, then
the creator cannot get the stake back, even if it is the winning edge.

Another case is if a layer-zero edge is created when there are no stake requirements and
then activated; the creator can get a refund even if he did not deposit any stake.

 function refundStake(bytes32 edgeId) public {
