The penalty calculation in the fast unlocking mechanism is incorrect and will charge users a
higher penalty than what they truly owe.

As shown in figure 11.1, the initiateFastUnlock function in the L2Staking contract
allows users to reduce the lock duration of their positions to three days. Users incur a
penalty for this action proportional to their locked amount and the remaining lock
duration.

 function initiateFastUnlock(uint256 lockId) public virtual returns (uint256) {
 ...
 // calculate penalty
 uint256 penalty = calculatePenalty(lock.amount, remainingLockingDuration(lock));

 uint256 amount = lock.amount - penalty;
 uint256 expDate = todayDay() + FAST_UNLOCK_DURATION;
 ...
 }

 Figure 11.1: The initiateFastUnlock function in L2Staking.sol#L293–296

However, the associated penalty calculation computes the penalty based on the remaining
days of the lock duration from when the user initiates the fast unlock request, including the
three-day period during which the position will still be locked.

