Finding: TLS listener thread does not time out
Severity: Medium
Difficulty: High
Type: Denial of Service

Description:
The TLS listener thread creates a new task for each new incoming connection. The task
reads a 4-byte length L and then waits for a message of length L from the network. If the
remote node sends less than L bytes, the thread will hang, waiting for the message to
complete. This ties up local resources and can be used to exhaust processing and memory
resources of the node.

