Insufficient access control checks in the supply_excess message handler of the
EvaaSYMinter contract allow anyone to mint an infinite number of Evaa SY tokens.

The FIVA protocol uses the EvaaSYMinter contract to allow users to mint SY tokens for
their Evaa deposits. Users transfer their base token to the EvaaSYMinter contract with the
wrap message as the forward_payload of the Jetton transfer message. The
EvaaSYMinter contract validates the transfer_notification message and transfers
the base token to the Evaa master contract with the supply_master message as the
forward_payload. The Evaa master contract updates the user deposit amount and sends
a supply_excess message to the EvaaSYMinter contract.

The EvaaSYMinter parses the custom payload included in the supply_excess message
and validates the message based on values included in the message. After validating the
message, the EvaaSYMinter contract mints the SY tokens to the recipient address
