Exploit Scenario
Bob wants to update his card limits, so he sends an op::update_limits message. He
does not remember his last sequence number, so he sets it to 4294967295, the maximum
value for a 32-bit unsigned integer.

When the operation is processed, limits_seqno is set to the value used in the message,
and the op::update_limits functionality is permanently broken, as there is no valid next
sequence number for updating the limits.

Recommendations:
Short term, enforce the sequence numbers to increase by one.

Long term, review every assumption or invariant in the system and ensure proper data
validation is performed. Improve the test suites with adversarial cases, and ensure that test
coverage is high enough for all files.

