Finding: Deployment process for card contracts can be vulnerable to front-running
Severity: Informational
Difficulty: Low
Type: Timing

Description:
holders-contracts/packages/ton/contracts/jetton-card-v3.fc

Description
The deployment and initialization process for card contracts is not necessarily atomic, as
not all the required state variables are stored in the contract deployment init data. To finish
the storage initialization, an op::deploy message is required.

If a contract’s deployment is done in a different transaction than the initialization, it is
possible for an attacker to initialize the contract storage with arbitrary values.

