Finding: Resource limits can be used to set arbitrary cgroup keys
Severity: Low
Difficulty: High
Type: Data Validation

Description:
Container configurations submitted to Styrolite can contain a set of key-value pairs of
cgroup settings intended to limit the target container’s resources. The resource limits are
added via push_resource_limit, which inserts arbitrary strings as key-value mappings:

 pub fn push_resource_limit(mut self, key: &str, value: &str) -> CreateRequestBuilder
 {
 if self.config.limits.is_none() {
 self.config.limits = BTreeMap::new().into();
 }
 if let Some(ref mut map) = self.config.limits {
 map.insert(key.to_string(), value.to_string());
 }
