Exploit Scenario
Mallory borrows 100 USDT from the Liquidium pool using profile X. She immediately
re-deposits the USDT into a separate profile Y. After 1 year, Mallory uses profile X to borrow
another 500 USDT. Assuming the pre-borrow interest rate is 5%, Mallory now owes 605
USDT in profile X.

Mallory’s large borrow causes the pool to go beyond the optimal liquidity point, driving the
USDT pool interest rate up to 25%. She then calls withdraw using profile Y, which triggers a
recomputation of the interest accrued to profile Y. She receives 125 USDT. Next, Mallory
repays 605 USDT to account X, plus some dust to cover one second of interest on the
balance.

After this sequence of operations, Mallory has earned a net income of just under 20 USDT,
taken from the Liquidium protocol funds.

