Finding: Borrow checks do not account for pending borrows
Severity: High
Difficulty: Medium
Type: Timing

Description:
When new borrow positions are opened, the protocol canister does not account for
pending borrows when checking liquidity limits. Borrows that cannot be confirmed may be
initiated; however, this failure occurs after funds have already been sent to the user.
Borrowed funds remain accounted for as pending outflows rather than debt. These
outflows can never be cleared, which prevents users from fully withdrawing all collateral
and prevents the protocol from accruing interest on the borrowed funds. These positions
also cannot be liquidated, which could cause the protocol to become insolvent.

