Cycle drain attacks can prevent liquidations and can also cause mid-transaction traps that
leave the system in inconsistent states that may be useful to an attacker.

Exploit Scenario
A malicious user wants to prevent liquidation. She adds a very large number of wallets and
then starts removing and re-adding a wallet repeatedly. Each removal uses a large number
of cycles such that she can drain cycles from the system without being blocked by
request-level rate limiting.

Recommendations:
