Finding: Use of incorrect loop break to handle add_to_store and handle_events failures
Severity: Informational
Difficulty: High
Type: Undefined Behavior

Description:
The Terminal code that executes event handlers (figure 3.1) uses a break to stop the
processing of events when an error occurs. However, because the break stops the for loop
instead of the outer loop, the events will continue to be processed. This could lead to an
undesirable node state.

Currently, the error can be caused only by a closed channel, which is considered a
programming mistake that should not ever happen. However, further developments in the
AlephBFT code could introduce additional error conditions more likely to trigger this issue.

