 Trail of Bits 12 DFINITY Fix Review
 PUBLIC
The canister will never be notified that the signing request failed and will be left waiting
indefinitely for the corresponding reply from the distributed signing service.

Fix Analysis
This issue has been fixed. It is now possible to set an expiry time for signing requests. If a
request has expired, it is removed from the set of ongoing signing requests in the
get_signing_requests function. Since signing requests are removed only once they
have been paired with a quadruple, the corresponding quadruple will be removed as well.
This ensures that the following invariants hold:

 1. If a quadruple fails to complete, it will eventually be dropped by the payload builder
 when the corresponding signature request expires.

 2. Quadruples are deterministically matched with signing requests, which ensures that
 a malicious user cannot influence how quadruples and signing requests are paired.

