The PriceOracleSentinel contract’s isBorrowAllowed and isLiquidationAllowed
functions return true only if a “grace period” has elapsed since the oracle’s last update.
Setting the grace period parameter too high could result in a denial-of-service condition.

The relevant code appears in figure 8.1. Both isBorrowAllowed and
